This PR will solve the problem stated in the PR description. Some observations/ NITS:

"Node runners who only have IPv6 are now required to override -rpcbind to only specify the working interface if they were not doing so already."

Isn't it more correct to say that: "Node runners who only have IPv6 are now required to override -rpcbind and -rpcallowip to only specify the working interface if they were not doing so already." Without -rpcallowip=::1 it will still fail.

The code will solve a ipv4 squatter situation, but not the case when there is a ipv6 sqatter and `localhost` is used for bitcoin-cli , 'bitcoin-cli -rpcconnect=localhost` tries [::1] before 127.0.0.1 . Not a blocker because 127.0.0.1 is explicitly used but just an observation.

Found a non-blocking NIT in the code, see below.
